# Repo-owned Caddy site snippet for the Search API (see ADR-0001).
#
# Imported by the RemoteServer-owned main Caddyfile, e.g.:
#   bgc.example.com {
#       import /opt/bgc/sites/bgc.caddy
#   }
# The main Caddyfile owns the domain/TLS block; this snippet owns only the
# reverse_proxy target, so it stays a same-shape drop-in regardless of what
# domain fronts it.
#
# CUTOVER CONTRACT (deploy/deploy.sh depends on this exact shape — do not
# reformat):
#   - Exactly one line matching `reverse_proxy bgc_searchapi_<color>:8080`.
#   - "Active Color" = the <color> captured from that line.
#   - deploy.sh detects it with:
#       grep -oP 'reverse_proxy bgc_searchapi_\K(blue|green)(?=:8080)' bgc.caddy
#   - Cutover = deploy.sh does an in-place substitution of blue<->green on
#     that line, then `caddy reload`. No other line in this file may match
#     the `reverse_proxy bgc_searchapi_(blue|green):8080` pattern.

reverse_proxy bgc_searchapi_blue:8080
